  E_min=0.990, C_max=0.000, Score=0.990
  Original:      An operator may drive on an improved shoulder to the right only if necessary and safe, and only for one of the listed purposes (stop/stand/park; accelerate before entering main lane; decelerate before right turn; pass a slowing/stopped/disabled/left-turning vehicle; allow faster vehicle to pass; traffic-control device; avoid collision).
  Reconstructed: If a vehicle is on a paved roadway and is driving on the right shoulder, the operator must use the shoulder only when that use is necessary and safe, and only for stopping, standing, or parking; accelerating before entering the main lane; decelerating before making a right turn; passing a vehicle that is slowing, stopped, disabled, or turning left; allowing a faster vehicle to pass; complying with a traffic-control device; or avoiding a collision.
  Rationale: Strong mutual entailment (E_min=0.99), low contradiction (C_max=0.00)

